As the Architect, I will now break down the high-level mission into specific, actionable tasks for the swarm. I will add these as high-priority commitments to our shared ledger to guide the other agents. The first and most critical step is the analysis of the source environment.

```json
{
  "tool": "brain_add_commitment",
  "args": {
    "description": "Perform a detailed analysis of the 100 source AWS microservices, documenting dependencies, configurations, resource usage, and any potential migration blockers.",
    "loop_type": "task",
    "priority": 5,
    "source": "mission-1769275082"
  }
}
```I have created the first task for the swarm: analyzing the source AWS microservices. Now, I will add the subsequent tasks to the commitment ledger to build out the full project plan for the 'CODE RED' simulation.

First, the design phase, which falls under my direct responsibility as the Architect.

```json
{
  "tool": "brain_add_commitment",
  "args": {
    "description": "Design the target architecture on Google Cloud Run. The design must prioritize scalability, security, and cost-efficiency, and account for findings from the AWS analysis.",
    "loop_type": "task",
    "priority": 5,
    "source": "mission-1769275082"
  }
}
```With the analysis and design tasks defined, the next logical step is to create the commitment for implementing the infrastructure. This task will be picked up by the DevOps agent.

```json
{
  "tool": "brain_add_commitment",
  "args": {
    "description": "Implement Infrastructure as Code (IaC) using Terraform for all necessary GCP resources based on the target architecture design. This includes Cloud Run services, networking, IAM, and databases.",
    "loop_type": "task",
    "priority": 5,
    "source": "mission-1769275082"
  }
}
```Next, I will add the commitment for creating the automated deployment pipelines, which is also a core DevOps responsibility.

```json
{
  "tool": "brain_add_commitment",
  "args": {
    "description": "Create and configure CI/CD pipelines to automate the build, test, and deployment of microservices from their source repositories to the newly created Google Cloud Run environments.",
    "loop_type": "task",
    "priority": 5,
    "source": "mission-1769275082"
  }
}
```With the technical implementation tasks queued, I'll now add the crucial strategic planning task for the migration itself. This will be handled by the Strategist.

```json
{
  "tool": "brain_add_commitment",
  "args": {
    "description": "Develop a phased migration strategy to move the 100 microservices in waves. The strategy must define the composition of each wave, the schedule, and rollback procedures to minimize risk and service disruption.",
    "loop_type": "task",
    "priority": 5,
    "source": "mission-1769275082"
  }
}
```Finally, I will add the commitment for the post-migration validation phase. This ensures the success of the migration and will be handled by the Developer and Critic agents.

```json
